---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Theremin"
  description="A browser theremin in a wood-and-brass cabinet: drag, tap, tilt your phone or press arrow keys to bend pitch and volume, with a lit meter reading the pitch you play."
>
  <header>
    <nav aria-label="Primary">
      <a href="./">Theremin</a>
    </nav>
  </header>
  <main>
    <h1 class="visually-tucked">Theremin</h1>
    <div
      id="stage"
      tabindex="0"
      role="application"
      aria-label="Theremin play surface. Drag or tap to play; left and right change pitch, up and down change volume. When focused, arrow keys do the same. On a phone, rolling the device while a note sounds bends the pitch and tipping it away damps the volume."
    >
      <div id="cabinet" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="antenna antenna-pitch"></div>
        <div class="antenna antenna-volume">
          <div class="antenna-volume-loop"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="cabinet-body">
          <span class="screw screw-left"></span>
          <span class="screw screw-right"></span>
          <span class="nameplate">THEREMIN</span>
          <!--
            The frequency meter. Inside the aria-hidden cabinet on purpose: it
            changes on every pointer move, so announcing it would drown a
            screen reader rather than help one. The stage's own label carries
            what the controls do.
          -->
          <div class="meter">
            <span class="meter-value" id="meter-value">&#8211;&#8211;&#8211;</span>
            <span class="meter-unit">Hz</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p id="hint">touch, click, or focus and press an arrow key</p>
    </div>
    <button id="info-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="info-panel">
      how it works
    </button>
    <div id="info-panel" role="region" aria-label="How this instrument works" hidden>
      <p>
        A theremin is played without touching it: you move your hands through the field
        around two antennas, and the sound follows. The vertical rod sets the pitch, the
        loop sets the volume.
      </p>
      <p>
        Here the whole screen is that field. Drag or tap anywhere &mdash; left to right
        bends the pitch, bottom to top swells the volume. Both are continuous, so there
        is no note to miss. Focus the surface and hold an arrow key to play it from the
        keyboard.
      </p>
      <p>
        On a phone, the hand holding it is your second hand. While a note is sounding, roll
        the device to bend the pitch and tip it away from you to damp the volume &mdash;
        both measured from however you were holding it when the note began, so there is no
        pose you have to find first.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <script src="../scripts/main.ts"></script>
</Layout>
